From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:05:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: leave a failed prepare retryable

When q6asm_dai_prepare() failed after the DSP stream was opened, it either returned with the stream still
open (media format block failure: only logged, no cleanup) or freed the audio client while the PCM stayed open.
The next prepare then failed: the session's stream was already open on the DSP (ADSP_EALREADY, 'DSP returned
error[9]'), and with the client freed every further prepare failed with 'private data null or audio client
freed' - capture stayed dead until a reboot. Seen on the Surface Duo when PipeWire's card profile was switched
off and on quickly.

Undo exactly what this prepare set up (routing, DSP stream, memory map) on every error path, keep the audio client
(close() frees it), and name the failing call (open_write or open_read) in the error message.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 709b4f331..854ed72c3 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -257,7 +257,8 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		dev_err(dev, "%s: q6asm_open_write failed\n", __func__);
+		dev_err(dev, "%s: q6asm_open_%s failed\n", __func__,
+			substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ? "write" : "read");
 		goto open_err;
 	}
 
@@ -286,19 +287,27 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 			q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
 
 	}
-	if (ret < 0)
-		dev_info(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed\n", __func__);
-	else
-		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		dev_err(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed\n", __func__);
+		goto format_err;
+	}
 
-	return ret;
+	prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
 
+	return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * Undo exactly what this prepare set up, so a later prepare can start again: the DSP stream must not stay
+	 * open (the next open of the session would fail with ADSP_EALREADY), and the audio client stays - it belongs
+	 * to the open PCM and is freed in close(). Freeing it here left every later prepare failing with "audio
+	 * client freed" until the PCM was closed, and the leaked DSP session kept failing after reopening.
+	 */
+format_err:
+	q6routing_stream_close(soc_prtd->dai_link->id, substream->stream);
 routing_err:
 	q6asm_cmd(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,  CMD_CLOSE);
 open_err:
 	q6asm_unmap_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client);
-	q6asm_audio_client_free(prtd->audio_client);
-	prtd->audio_client = NULL;
 
 	return ret;
 }
